   "text": {
    "L1": "The solar system is the Sun and everything that goes around it. It includes eight planets, moons, dwarf planets, asteroids and comets.",
    "L2": "A planet is not a star. Stars make their own light, but planets usually shine by reflecting sunlight.",
    "L3": "Starting at the Sun, the first four planets are Mercury, Venus, Earth and Mars.",
    "L4": "After Mars come Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus and Neptune. This gives all eight planets in order.",
    "L5": "Use this memory sentence: My Very Educated Mother Just Served Us Noodles. Its initials match the planets.",
    "L6": "Jupiter is the largest planet, and Mercury is the smallest. The Sun is far bigger than all of them.",
    "L7": "Venus can look like a morning or evening star, but it is a planet. It shines steadily, while stars twinkle.",
    "L8": "Seasons are caused by Earth's tilted axis, not its distance from the Sun. Never look directly at the Sun."
   },
